          ":question/id": "09e95d08-30a6-5777-a8a8-348db8bfab42",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131724",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=2 \\\\ -3x-4y &=3 \\\\ 2x-4y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-5,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement \u201cThe system is inconsistent\u201d is true."
        },
