          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-74637",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=-1 \\\\ x-2y &=1 \\\\ -x-5y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & \u2194{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 7y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-\\frac{3}{7}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2\\left(-\\frac{3}{7}\\right)=1\\,\u27f9\\,x=\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\n \nSo, we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement \u201cThe system is consistent independent\u201d is true."
        },
