          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131718",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=2 \\\\ -2x+7y+2z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement \u201cThe system is consistent dependent\u201d is true."
        },
