          ":question/id": "35b0295d-1e16-59cc-a201-696e791e0b7d",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-74643",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=8 \\\\ x+y &=-2 \\\\ x+\\frac{1}{2}y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & \u2194{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=-2 \\\\ -y &=14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-14.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-14)=-2\\,\u27f9\\,x=12.\n$$\n\n \nSo,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent.   \n\nAs a result, only statement \u201cThe system is consistent independent\u201d is true."
        },
