          ":question/id": "cd791ebf-f827-5528-ae25-d3ac1f74c5cc",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131720",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y-2z &=4 \\\\ 3x-9y-3z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -6 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -6 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement \u201cThe system is consistent dependent\u201d is true."
