          ":question/id": "b9b47374-5548-52b6-9b51-17d923fcd37b",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131721",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 3x+7y &=1 \\\\ -2x-4y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ y &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=4$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=-9.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement \u201cThe system is consistent independent\u201d is true."
        },
