          ":question/id": "a8971116-e24d-5808-9b29-a50e168511e5",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-74634",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=-1 \\\\ 2x-4y &=3 \\\\ x+y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we will first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=\\frac{9}{2},$ and it has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement \u201cThe system is inconsistent\u201d is true."
