          ":question/id": "22d64530-5ce7-515c-aafe-c528e2fc812f",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-74834",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-1 \\\\ 2x-7y &=0 \\\\ -4x+15y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\n\nII. The system has no solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent dependent",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-1 \\\\ y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=2$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=7.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."
        },
