          ":question/id": "2f4a72f8-3bd3-5788-9d12-62ca6f611891",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-74636",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+y &=-1 \\\\ 2x+3y &=3 \\\\ -x-4y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is inconsistent\n\nII. The system has a unique solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent dependent",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-1,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."
        },
