          ":question/id": "d63c26b5-97c7-566b-af91-3b869e17916f",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-74638",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=-3 \\\\ -6x-4y &=6,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\n\nII. The system is consistent dependent\n\nIII. The system has no solution",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find the solution to the system. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n3x+2y=-3\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."
        }
