          {
            ":db/id": 17592186116122,
            ":step/content": {
              ":db/id": 17592186116494,
              ":tutorial/content": "Recall that a system of linear equations is called **consistent** if it has at least one solution. Otherwise, if there are no solutions, the system is called **inconsistent**. \n\nFor a consistent system, \n\n- the system is called **consistent independent** if the solution is unique, while\n\n- the system is called **consistent dependent** if there are infinitely many solutions.\n\n![](images/f5/f5b808eac6e1d865b13b68ce2a4f7d317560ae3965928e478531fcd2148c2c6b.png)",
              ":tutorial/id": "e0c85152-daea-5a87-a3ba-81870558c7a2",
              ":tutorial/math-academy-id": 3163,
              ":tutorial/title": "Consistent and Inconsistent Systems of Linear Equations"
            },
            ":step/id": "2fa6eba1-6298-51b5-bbc9-bd8c46a79468",
